  m_Color: {r: 0.19607843, g: 0.19607843, b: 0.19607843, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_FontData:
    m_Font: {fileID: 12800000, guid: 5e66e77026a31924e936fc62ef1e97b9, type: 3}
    m_FontSize: 34
    m_FontStyle: 3
    m_BestFit: 0
    m_MinSize: 2
    m_MaxSize: 80
    m_Alignment: 1
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1.5
  m_Text: 'Dear Seraphina,



    I often find myself pondering the path my life
    would have taken had we never crossed paths. Without your unwavering belief in
    my musical talent, I fear I would have remained a mere painter, my canvases filled
    with silent colors instead of the symphonies that now resonate within my soul.
    Your influence ignited a fire within me, a passion that has defined my existence.*



    This
    excerpt establishes the composer''s gratitude towards Seraphina while subtly
    hinting at an alternative career path. The line "I would have remained a mere
    painter" clearly indicates that the composer considered art before dedicating
    himself to music.

'
